#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111770} :activity/id #uuid "0be09731-4b99-5a42-a70e-c1f672108f62" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048360 :topic/id #uuid "9894c8b0-6628-5c7a-b1f4-a6bfebc14d33" :topic/math-academy-id 1461} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111429 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111858 :tutorial/content "The diagonals of a rectangle are equal and bisect each other. Consequently, they divide a rectangle into four isosceles triangles, as shown below.\n\n![](images/4f/4f0aafdf04bb7f967122fc8f90454b1b09787e375857bac3bcf5fdf80925e32c.png)\n\nIn a square, the diagonals also bisect the angles.\n\n![](images/cd/cd61fabe993fa6cde5ea4020a659e86b3543597d70a304b3e5ada3abfa426186.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "4643230c-067e-5817-af66-88717e7b8c66" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2357 :tutorial/title "The Diagonals of Rectangles and Squares"} :step/id #uuid "11275c8d-5eda-5537-b710-43e9d7986214" :step/math-academy-id 10171 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111773}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111770 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111848 :tutorial/content "A **rectangle** is a parallelogram where all angles are right. It has all the properties of parallelograms: its opposite sides are parallel and congruent.\n\n![](images/1f/1fa96b5993a48483798ff4ac05d75f1ffa271f82e5ed6e61a452eb97b3daf3e4.png)\n\nIf all $4$ sides of a rectangle are congruent, then it is a **square**.\n\n![](images/82/822788813f0e81eebef50f324e1bcaf329e7fa5552e10557a19d20b4e868063e.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "1fb26940-464f-55d2-9903-b4695c595b5f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2270 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "337c70d4-a057-5cca-a1b3-1b562ca18243" :step/math-academy-id 9475 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111771}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111771 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110780 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110409 :question/id #uuid "b5149f89-fb8c-5a67-9cd6-08742f659b57" :question/math-academy-id "e-2850"}